WEBVTT

00:05:27.717 --> 00:05:31.604
Now, with the original description
in the 18th century,

00:05:31.628 --> 00:05:33.443
Charles Bonnet did not have them.

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:36.209
His grandfather had these hallucinations.

00:05:36.233 --> 00:05:39.573
His grandfather was
a magistrate, an elderly man.

00:05:39.597 --> 00:05:41.830
He'd had cataract surgery.

00:05:41.854 --> 00:05:44.105
His vision was pretty poor.

00:05:44.129 --> 00:05:49.294
And in 1759, he described to his grandson

00:05:49.318 --> 00:05:51.635
various things he was seeing.

00:05:51.659 --> 00:05:55.107
The first thing he said
was he saw a handkerchief in midair.

00:05:55.131 --> 00:05:58.976
It was a large blue handkerchief
with four orange circles.

00:05:59.456 --> 00:06:01.827
And he knew it was a hallucination.